      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=-3{x}^{2}-18x+7.$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=-3$ and $b=-18$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-18)}{2(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-18)}{(-6)} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-3.$",
